{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
    "name": "BP Industrial Portal – Broker Home API",
    "description": "End-to-end collection for the Broker Home page APIs.\n\n**Flow**\n1. Run **Auth / Broker Login** — the test script extracts the JWT and stores it as `{{token}}`.\n2. Every subsequent request automatically attaches `Bearer {{token}}` via the collection-level auth.\n3. The **Unauthorized** folder verifies that every endpoint returns 401 when no token is supplied.\n\n**Variable**\n| Variable | Default | Set by |\n|---|---|---|\n| `baseUrl` | `http://localhost:5128` | Manual (change per environment) |\n| `token` | _(empty)_ | Auto-set by Broker Login test script |",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:5128",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Base URL of the running API. Change to your Azure URL for cloud testing."
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "JWT Bearer token. Auto-populated by the Broker Login request."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Broker Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status 200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Response time < 3s', () => pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(3000));",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Token is returned', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('token');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.token).to.be.a('string').and.not.be.empty;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Role is Broker', () => pm.expect(body.role).to.equal('Broker'));",
                  "pm.test('UserId is present', () => pm.expect(body.userId).to.be.a('number').and.above(0));",
                  "pm.test('Username is present', () => pm.expect(body.username).to.be.a('string').and.not.be.empty);",
                  "",
                  "// Auto-store token for all subsequent requests",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', body.token);",
                  "pm.test('Token saved to collection variable', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.collectionVariables.get('token')).to.not.be.empty;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"emailId\": \"Alexjohn@bp.com\",\n  \"password\": \"admin1234\",\n  \"isBroker\": true\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/Login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "Login"]
            },
            "description": "Authenticates as a Broker user and stores the returned JWT as `{{token}}`.\n\nCredentials: `Alexjohn@bp.com` / `admin1234`"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
